{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Once two strangers [G]climbed ole [D]Rocky Top [Bm]lookin' for a [A]moonshine [D]still.
[D]Strangers ain't come [G]down from [D]Rocky Top, [Bm]reckon they [A]never [D]will.
[D]Corn won't grow at [G]all on [D]Rocky Top, [Bm]dirt's too [A]rocky by [D]far.
[D]That's why all the [G]folks on [D]Rocky Top [Bm]get their [A]corn from a [D]jar.

{comment: Chorus}
{comment: Break}

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]I've had years of [G]cramped up [D]city life; [Bm]stuck like a [A]duck in a [D]pen.
[D]All I know is [G]it's a pity [D]life can't be [Bm]simple a[A]gain.[D]

{comment: Chorus}
